## BuildKit per-Dockerfile override (named <dockerfile>.dockerignore): used only when building
## Dockerfile.spike-hdr. Same as .dockerignore except it keeps tests/resources/hdr/ in the build
## context, so the spike image can bake in the real local fixtures directly -- no volume mount,
## no extra compose wiring. The real Dockerfile/.dockerignore pair is untouched: fixture bytes
## never enter the production image.
.env*
!.env.example
node_modules/
.svelte-kit/
build/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.cache/
.planning/
.opencode/
.claude/
.agents/
*.log
SPEC.md
tests/resources/heic-test-set/
